lisa-addressed:
BUGFIX: catalog children listed grouped controls at the catalog level too, so controls appeared twice (once under the catalog, once under their group) in tree/graph. Cause: GORM Preload("Controls") on a Catalog returns EVERY control by catalog_id (grouped ones included), so catalogTopControls wrongly held group members. Fix in loadCatalogs: build the group-membership set first, then catalogTopControls = catalog controls NOT in any group; catalogAllControls now dedups (group controls + only-ungrouped controls). Verified on live data (catalog f47..401: was 8 groups + ~10 duplicated controls -> now 8 groups, 0 top-level controls, no overlap with group children). Added integration test TestLineageGrouping.

lisa-design:
Risk/evidence lineage nodes enriched for tree+graph rendering. LineageNode gained (all omitempty): relationship (edge type from parent: group|control|implements|documents|has-risk|has-evidence — for graph edge styling), and risk-node detail severity/score/likelihood/impact/linkedEvidenceCount + reviewDeadline/lastReviewedAt/firstSeenAt/lastSeenAt, and evidence-node detail reason/collectedAt(end)/expires. severityForScore bands the 1-25 likelihood×impact score (<=2 negligible, <=5 low, <=11 moderate, <=19 high, else critical) for node coloring; UI may re-band. Deliberately did NOT add owner/sourceType/descriptions/labels (user: keep it lean, dates & deadlines only). control->control children are split into ImplementsChildren (relationship=implements) then DocumentsChildren (documents) so each edge is labelled. Evidence collectedAt = latest evidence "end"; reason = status->>'reason'. No schema changes — all fields already in risks/evidences models.
